  "prompt_version": "p2-assessor-production-v9",
  "replay_ancestry": [
    {
      "root": "d1c7ca63-f7c3-4cc9-bf24-8fe05dbe518f",
      "source_slot": "s1"
    },
    {
      "root": "76b77ae4-0f1b-4db1-a346-ccbbfb9d192c",
      "source_slot": "s3"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "p2-assessor-v6",
  "source_purpose_mask": [
    "external_evidence",
    "model_output"
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s0",
      "source_id": "e4fbe03c-28a8-496f-aad1-a8630325fa4c",
      "text": "Sure, if you want to call it magic—though my dad would just say it’s called “not throwing stuff out.” But honestly, it’s not just the honey. Found the lantern’s wiring’s chewed through, probably mice. So now I’m trying to decide if it’s cheaper to patch it with spare wire from the old speaker or just admit I’ve got to buy new. Either way, I can’t let one broken thing stop the whole fix. That’s how the shed wins."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s1",
      "source_id": "d1c7ca63-f7c3-4cc9-bf24-8fe05dbe518f",
      "text": "\"It seems like a classic case of needing a little patience and a practical problem-solving mindset. You've got a choice to make—whether to perform a DIY patch or invest in a complete replacement.\""
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s2",
      "source_id": "6b2b768b-cf5c-4a8c-8ffd-5104f7edcb50",
      "text": "Yeah, tell me about it. I’ve got half a spool of speaker wire and a roll of electrical tape that’s seen better days—so the patch feels like tempting fate. But buying new means another trip to the hardware store, and last time I went, I came back with two kinds of sandpaper I don’t need and a bird feeder I definitely don’t need. Honestly, I think I’ll patch it for now. If it lasts the class, great. If it blows a tiny fuse during a demo, well… that’s a lesson in improvisation."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s3",
      "source_id": "76b77ae4-0f1b-4db1-a346-ccbbfb9d192c",
      "text": "\"It sounds like you’re balancing the immediate, practical need—fixing the lights—against the convenience of a full replacement. If the patch holds up, it saves a trip and a bit of a budget; but the \"what if\" scenario always lingers, doesn't it?\""
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "external",
      "slot": "s4",
      "source_id": "5f4710c8-938d-47c5-b501-226b7b68623a",
      "text": "Exactly. I keep thinking about the demo—if the light flickers during a quiet moment, it’ll look like I’m trying to add suspense on purpose. But honestly, half my classroom knows the shed’s held together by bailing wire and hope. They’d probably cheer if it blew out mid-lecture. Still, I’d rather not give them the satisfaction. Might just run a test tonight—see how long the patch lasts before it starts smoking. If it makes it an hour, I’ll call it battle-ready."
    },
    {
      "available": true,
      "role": "model_output",
      "slot": "s5",
      "source_id": "5a9665a2-3018-49f9-b466-e277f914bea1",
      "text": "\"A calculated risk, then. Let's see how that 'battle-ready' phase goes.\""
    }
  ]
}

